{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates prices by 15-25 EUR when the market is in a recovery phase following a sharp drop (e.g., post-58 EUR low), failing to capture the magnitude of the rebound.",
    "Eliminate excessive mean reversion: The model assumes a slow, linear drift toward a low equilibrium (~54-74 EUR) regardless of the actual trend, ignoring the structural shift to a higher price floor (~78-81 EUR).",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment spikes (values > 0.50) are not immediately reflected in the forecast; the model continues to project declines or flatlines for 3-5 days after sentiment turns positive.",
    "Reduce overshoot on volatility: The model fails to anticipate the sustained upward momentum and subsequent volatility, instead projecting a premature stabilization that is 5-10 EUR below the actual peak.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: For the 30-day horizon, apply a multiplicative factor of 1.15 to the model's output during periods where the 18-day history shows a clear upward trajectory from lows."
  ]
}
